@* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Site/Account/UserProfile.aspx (+ .aspx.cs) -> Components/Pages/Site/Account/UserProfile.razor
   (checklist task 97). The route is the one the migrated layouts link to (Specialist 5).

   The .aspx markup is ported faithfully: MasterPageFile="~/BackendMaster.Master" ->
   @layout BackendLayout, the Script/StyleSheet/BottomScript <asp:Content> blocks were EMPTY -> no
   <SectionContent>, and the body was

       <h2><em>I'm under development.</em></h2>
       <asp:PlaceHolder runat="server" ID="Placeholder1"></asp:PlaceHolder>

   Placeholder1 was never populated by any code in the solution (re-grepped), so it rendered
   nothing -- and nothing is emitted for it here.

   THE emailLinkButton SURFACE. The code-behind declared

       public LinkButton emailLinkButton;

   and its only handler, EmailReportLinkButton_Click, was COMMENTED OUT in the original source.
   The field was never instantiated and never added to the control tree, so the page emitted no
   link at all. Both halves of that are preserved deliberately:
     * the surface still exists, as the anchor below plus the EmailLinkButtonVisible flag that
       gates it -- an ancestor/derived page can switch it on exactly as WebForms code could have
       added the LinkButton to the placeholder;
     * it is INERT. There is no click handler, because the original had none (it was commented
       out), and no behaviour is invented. It is not a stub: there is no NotImplementedException
       and nothing to implement -- the dead end is the original behaviour.
     * it renders NOTHING by default, which is what the never-added LinkButton rendered.
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- *@
@page "/Site/Account/UserProfile"
@layout BackendLayout
@inherits MixERPAuthorizedPageBase

<h2><em>I'm under development.</em></h2>

@if (this.EmailLinkButtonVisible)
{
    @* The LinkButton's rendering: <a id="..."> with its text and NO behaviour. *@
    <a id="emailLinkButton" href="#" @onclick:preventDefault>@Titles.Email</a>
}

@code {
    /// <summary>
    ///     Whether the <c>emailLinkButton</c> surface is rendered. FALSE by default, because the
    ///     legacy <c>public LinkButton emailLinkButton</c> was declared but never added to
    ///     Placeholder1, so the page rendered no link.
    /// </summary>
    protected bool EmailLinkButtonVisible { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    ///     Page_Init: <c>this.IsLandingPage = true</c> -- the profile page has no menu entry of its
    ///     own, so the policy check must not run against it. Set in the constructor because the
    ///     base activation sequence that reads it runs in OnInitializedAsync.
    /// </summary>
    public UserProfile()
    {
        this.IsLandingPage = true;
    }
}
